[center][size=6][b]KNOX ATLAS[/b][/size][/center]
[center][size=4][i]A friendly, read-only companion atlas for Project Zomboid.[/i][/size][/center]
[center][url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Project-Zomboid-Interactive-Map/releases][b]DOWNLOAD LATEST RELEASE[/b][/url]  |  [url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Project-Zomboid-Interactive-Map][b]VIEW SOURCE ON GITHUB[/b][/url][/center]

Knox Atlas is a standalone Windows companion application that turns the map data already installed with Project Zomboid into a fast, modern desktop atlas. Use it to find towns, streets, businesses, building types, likely resources, possible vehicle zones, and useful world coordinates while you play.

[b]Knox Atlas is read-only.[/b] It does not install into Project Zomboid, modify the game, or write into your saves. It reads the local Steam installation and limited save metadata, then stores personal markers and preferences in its own application storage.

[line]

[size=5][b]✨ Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]🗺️ [b]Game-derived map[/b] — water, terrain, roads, railways, buildings, towns, landmarks, and street names are read from the files installed with the game.
[*]🔎 [b]Search and coordinate travel[/b] — find places by name or jump directly to an X/Y coordinate.
[*]🏪 [b]Expandable filters[/b] — focus on individual business, building, likely-loot, resource, and vehicle categories.
[*]🎒 [b]Honest loot hints[/b] — useful zones are clearly labeled as likely locations, not guaranteed live inventory.
[*]🚙 [b]Drivable vehicle pools[/b] — inspect possible car, van, truck, utility, and emergency vehicle spawn areas.
[*]📍 [b]Named custom markers[/b] — save up to 100 colored points locally and keep them visible across the map.
[*]🧭 [b]Simple navigation[/b] — set a manual position and destination, see direct tile distance, copy coordinates, and save a favorite center/zoom view.
[*]🖥️ [b]Second-monitor friendly[/b] — a clean desktop interface designed to stay useful beside the game.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]⬇️ Installation[/b][/size]

Knox Atlas is a standalone companion, not an in-game mod. Do not place it in the Project Zomboid Mods folder.

[list]
[*][b]Installer — recommended:[/b] download and run the setup .exe, then launch Knox Atlas from the normal Windows shortcut.
[*][b]Portable ZIP — optional:[/b] extract the entire archive into a writable folder and run Knox-Atlas.exe. Keep the included files together.
[/list]

The portable package expects the Microsoft WebView2 runtime to already be installed. The installer is the easiest choice for most users. Project Zomboid must be installed through Steam in a standard library location for the current release to discover its map automatically.

[b][color=#d99b55]🛡️ Antivirus / SmartScreen:[/color][/b] Knox Atlas is not currently code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen or antivirus software may warn about an unfamiliar or unsigned application. This is common for small independent projects, but please download files only from this Nexus page or the official GitHub Releases page. The complete source and release workflow are public on GitHub; you are warmly invited to inspect them or build the application yourself. If a warning looks unusual or you are uncertain about a file, do not run it until you are comfortable with its source.

[line]

[size=5][b]🗺️ What the layers mean[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Basemap, streets, buildings, and official labels[/b] come directly from the installed game files.
[*][b]Businesses and likely loot[/b] are broad hints inferred from game-authored zones. Actual items are not guaranteed.
[*][b]Vehicle pools[/b] are places where drivable vehicles may spawn, not confirmed live vehicles.
[*][b]Latest save location[/b] is the last saved in-game map view, not the player's live position.
[*][b]Custom markers[/b] are created by you and stored locally by Knox Atlas, never in the Project Zomboid save.
[/list]

Random generation, sandbox settings, mods, player activity, and the current save determine what is actually present in the world.

[line]

[size=5][b]📌 Current scope — v0.1.0[/b][/size]

The first release targets Windows and the base English map in common Steam library locations. It does not currently track live players, read live container inventories, locate vehicle keys, identify randomized survivor houses, or automatically merge enabled map mods.

Those limits are deliberate. Knox Atlas only presents information when its source and certainty can be explained honestly.

[line]

